{"chunk_id": "21419cd053ba", "text": "After Bhishma falls and lies upon his self-chosen bed of arrows, physicians arrive but he refuses treatment, declaring that a Kshatriya who has reached such a state should not seek healing. Both Kauravas and Pandavas, moved by his steadfast adherence to warrior ideals, honor him and withdraw for the night. The next day kings, citizens, performers, and crowds gather as if attending a sacred spectacle, united in reverence despite the war. Tormented by thirst yet rejecting ordinary comforts, Bhishma asks specifically for Arjuna. Understanding his grandsire\u2019s wish, Arjuna shoots a divine arrow into the earth, releasing a cool, celestial spring that refreshes Bhishma. The miraculous act amazes all present and momentarily unites the warring hosts in awe.\nBhishma, lying on his bed of arrows, refuses treatment; Arjuna shoots an arrow into the earth to produce a divine stream of water for him.\nThemes: heroic honor, warrior ethics, reverence for elders, divine weapons, momentary truce", "vector": [0.007025199942290783, -0.005075239576399326, 0.005616153124719858, 0.014183958992362022, -0.0022705020383000374, 0.02311905100941658, -0.012614641338586807, -0.015746599063277245, -0.01945953629910946, -0.020087264478206635, 0.010925120674073696, 0.007686316967010498, -0.0017479525413364172, 0.009536108002066612, -0.0014791652793064713, -0.006277270149439573, 0.044314853847026825, -0.009776514023542404, 0.039079345762729645, -0.02111566811800003, 2.022948319790885e-05, 0.013703146949410439, -0.0007178792729973793, 0.021048888564109802, -0.026057347655296326, 0.013155555352568626, 0.01575995422899723, -0.01982014626264572, -0.006965098436921835, -0.020020484924316406, -0.021502988412976265, 0.0032755329739302397, -0.021356074139475822, 0.01210043951869011, -0.046745628118515015, 0.003826463595032692, -0.010945155285298824, -0.017135610803961754, 0.019339334219694138, -0.007192148827016354, 0.0029683473985642195, -0.019232487305998802, -0.0